    "answer": {
      "short": "In column order (4, 3, 2, 1 significant figures):\n\n$274.62$: $2.746\\times10^2$, $2.75\\times10^2$, $2.7\\times10^2$, $3\\times10^2$.\n\n$0.041236$: $4.124\\times10^{-2}$, $4.12\\times10^{-2}$, $4.1\\times10^{-2}$, $4\\times10^{-2}$.\n\n$1704.28$: $1.704\\times10^3$, $1.70\\times10^3$, $1.7\\times10^3$, $2\\times10^3$.\n\n$1.9925\\times10^{27}$: $1.993\\times10^{27}$, $1.99\\times10^{27}$, $2.0\\times10^{27}$, $2\\times10^{27}$.",
      "worked": "Write each number in scientific notation, then round the coefficient independently to each requested precision. Keep trailing zeros when they indicate significant figures.\n\n$274.62=2.7462\\times10^2$. Rounding the coefficient to 4, 3, 2 and 1 significant figures gives $2.746$, $2.75$, $2.7$ and $3$, respectively. Thus the row is $2.746\\times10^2$, $2.75\\times10^2$, $2.7\\times10^2$, $3\\times10^2$.\n\n$0.041236=4.1236\\times10^{-2}$. Rounding the coefficient gives $4.124$, $4.12$, $4.1$ and $4$. Thus the row is $4.124\\times10^{-2}$, $4.12\\times10^{-2}$, $4.1\\times10^{-2}$, $4\\times10^{-2}$.\n\n$1704.28=1.70428\\times10^3$. Rounding the coefficient gives $1.704$, $1.70$, $1.7$ and $2$. Thus the row is $1.704\\times10^3$, $1.70\\times10^3$, $1.7\\times10^3$, $2\\times10^3$.\n\n$1.9925\\times10^{27}$ is already in scientific notation. Rounding its coefficient gives $1.993$, $1.99$, $2.0$ and $2$. Thus the row is $1.993\\times10^{27}$, $1.99\\times10^{27}$, $2.0\\times10^{27}$, $2\\times10^{27}$.",
